<section class="section wrap content-page"><div class="prose">
<p><strong>35+ years in finance, manufacturing operations and business systems.</strong></p>
<p>I work with owners, managing directors and CEOs of established mid-sized businesses, especially owner-managed and family businesses in manufacturing, processing, FMCG, distribution and trading. I work remotely from Kenya, with a focus on Kenya and East Africa, and take on selected assignments in the UK and other markets.</p>
<h2 id="business-performance-reviews">Business Performance Reviews</h2>
<p>When sales grow and margins fall, I examine where the margin is going and which products, customers or costs are driving the decline.</p>
<p>At Pwani Oil Products, I developed management and exception reports for the Board and department heads. I introduced Value Addition per Kg to help management assess profitability and the Bulk-to-Consumer Ratio to track changes in product mix.</p>
<h2 id="business-analysis-strategy">Business Analysis &amp; Strategy</h2>
<p>If you’re weighing an expansion or a pricing change, I can help you compare the options and test the assumptions before you commit resources.</p>
<p>At Pwani Oil Products, I prepared the feasibility studies for two major expansions. The studies supported syndicated bank financing for both projects.</p>
<h2 id="information-systems-process-improvement">Information Systems &amp; Process Improvement</h2>
<p>When departments report different stock figures or month-end reporting depends on manual spreadsheet reconciliations, I trace how the information is captured and passed between teams. That helps establish what your existing software can handle and where a change in process or system would help.</p>
<p>At Comcraft Services, I took over a stalled IMPACT ENCORE implementation and completed the rollout across five Aluminium Group companies. At Pwani Oil Products, I led pre-ERP planning for the Oracle E-Business Suite rollout.</p>
<h2>Operating experience</h2>
<p>At E.A. Match, I progressed from Accountant to General Manager and spent more than five years managing three manufacturing units, a trading operation and a workshop profit centre.</p>
<h2 id="how-i-work">How we would work together</h2>
<ol><li>Tell me what you want to understand or decide, what information you have and when you need an answer.</li><li>I’ll tell you whether I can help and what I would examine.</li><li>If we decide to proceed, we’ll agree the scope, what you’ll receive and the timeframe before work begins.</li></ol>
